                        "entry_id": "33f5fbf1-45ac-33ef-9a10-0a0fbc813415",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A bumblebee."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11d50335-cc6b-4d1c-b7c3-657c87016546",
                                "sense_id": "c63ce3eb-5623-319e-928a-88f7bfe49135",
                                "text": "The Fox, the Ape, and the Humble-Bee,\nWere ſtill at oddes being but three."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd658ba0-6f09-4b5b-9616-9d0538caaed7",
                                "sense_id": "c63ce3eb-5623-319e-928a-88f7bfe49135",
                                "text": "1800's, Ralph Waldo Emerson, The Humblebee\nBurly, dozing humblebee,\nWhere thou art is clime for me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "add93260-ae3c-45b0-8277-8d4294f6fd40",
                                "sense_id": "c63ce3eb-5623-319e-928a-88f7bfe49135",
                                "text": "Hence I have very little doubt, that if the whole genus of humble-bees became extinct or very rare in England, the heartsease and red clover would become very rare, or wholly disappear."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
